# ============================================================
#  .gitignore  —  cs-notebook
# ============================================================

# ---------- Rust ----------

# Cargo build output. Regenerated by `cargo build` / `cargo check` / `cargo run`.
# Matches `target/` at any depth, so every crate in the repo is covered:
#   Rust/target/  Rust/hello_cargo/target/  Rust/guessing_game/target/
# This is the big one — it is ~70 MB of compiler artifacts right now.
target/

# Leftover files from `rustc --backtrace` / backups made by editors
**/*.rs.bk

# Standalone `rustc main.rs` output (no cargo involved)
*.pdb
/Rust/main

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored:
# these are binary crates, and Cargo's own guidance is to commit the lockfile
# for binaries so everyone builds the exact same dependency versions.

# ---------- OS junk ----------

.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------- Editor / IDE ----------

*.swp
*.swo
*.sublime-workspace
*~
.idea/

# VS Code: keep .vscode/ tracked if you want shared settings.
# Uncomment to ignore your personal (non-shared) config instead:
# .vscode/launch.json
# .vscode/ipch/

# ---------- Secrets / local env ----------

.env
.env.local
*.local

# ---------- Notebook scratch ----------

# Jupyter checkpoints (if this notebook repo grows Python cells)
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------- Logs / temp ----------

*.log
tmp/
temp/
